OL,3,GNEWSAChildhood dementia needs
OL,4,Arecognition, family says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of a two-year-old girl
OL,7,Fdiagnosed with a form of childhood
OL,8,Fdementia has said she wants greater
OL,9,Frecognition of the term after their
OL,10,Fshock at what they felt was a lack of
OL,11,Fawareness.
OL,13,FEmily's daughter, Leni, was diagnosed
OL,14,Fwith Sanfilippo Syndrome last year - a
OL,15,Frare, genetic disorder which leads to
OL,16,Fsevere cognitive decline and a loss of
OL,17,Fmotor skills.
OL,19,FEmily, from Sevenoaks in Kent, said:
OL,20,F"It is catastrophic, I can't think of a
OL,21,Fworse diagnosis for your child, or for
OL,22,Fanyone, and yet no-one knows about it."
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
